{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Makholah</b> — it is a <i>po'el-et</i> form. Its meaning: one whose hope is drawn out — HaShem draws it out and he cannot attain the hope — it gives illness to the heart of the one who waits." "<b>And a tree of life</b> — like a healing tree, so is the desire of the one who desires, when it comes to him. And it is possible that it refers to one who gathers by hand."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "Resolved השם as HaShem per voice rules; the subject of 'draws it out' is left ambiguous as in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:32.822711026Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}